{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "houseiq-api-collection",
    "name": "HouseIQ API",
    "description": "Full HouseIQ backend collection for local development.\n\n## Setup\n1. Import `HouseIQ.postman_collection.json` and `HouseIQ.local.postman_environment.json`.\n2. Select the **HouseIQ Local** environment.\n3. Ensure Auth0 test credentials are in the environment (`auth0Domain`, `auth0ClientId`, `auth0ClientSecret`, user A/B username+password).\n   These mirror `AUTH0_TEST_*` from `backend/.env` (Resource Owner Password grant).\n4. Ensure the backend is running on `http://localhost:5000`.\n\n## Auth (automatic)\nCollection pre-request scripts fetch/refresh `accessToken` and `accessTokenUserB` via Auth0 password-realm grant.\nTokens are cached until near expiry — you should not need to paste Bearer tokens manually.\n\n## IDs (automatic where possible)\n- `GET /api/homes` / `POST /api/homes` set `homeId`\n- `GET/POST documents` set `ownedDocumentId` / `deletableDocumentId`\n- Part 19 delete sets `deletedDocumentId`\n- `userBDocumentId` still needs a document owned by User B (upload while using User B, or set once)\n\n## Document ownership suite\nRun folder **07 Document Ownership (Parts 15-19)** after `homeId` + document ids exist.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:5000"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "01 Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET / — Backend health",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/",
            "description": "Confirms the Express server is reachable."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Reports backend is running', function () {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.message).to.include('HouseIQ backend is running');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "02 Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /api/auth/me — Current user",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me",
            "description": "Requires a valid Auth0 Bearer token. Returns the authenticated Auth0 user id."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('User is authenticated', function () {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.authenticated).to.eql(true);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.auth0UserId).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /api/auth/me — Missing token (401)",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me",
            "description": "Confirms requireAuth rejects unauthenticated calls."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 401', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "03 Homes",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /api/homes — List homes",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/homes",
            "description": "Lists homes. After a successful response, copies the first home id into `homeId` when that variable is empty."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const homes = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Returns an array', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(homes).to.be.an('array');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "if (Array.isArray(homes) && homes.length > 0 && !pm.environment.get('homeId')) {",
                  "  pm.environment.set('homeId', homes[0].id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /api/homes — Create home",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Postman Test Home\",\n  \"yearBuilt\": 1998,\n  \"notes\": \"Created from the HouseIQ Postman collection\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/homes",
            "description": "Creates a home and stores its id in `homeId`."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const home = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (home && home.id) {",
                  "  pm.environment.set('homeId', home.id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
